# lazily-prefers-fewer: `text lazily` swaps its `split`'s targets, so it
# prefers to match less, and `<"<", text lazily, ">">` over "<a> <b>" gives
# two matches, each ending at the first ">" it can (spec chapter 4,
# Elements; chapter 8, Compiling). The greedy-by-default case is its pair.
# The matches are pinned. Its Fuel, allocation and state figures are Cost
# Model 0's, as the TS Core blessed them.

> load search identity=8be578bce0b73d8fe0d29a6b33ff8990747e670c9d87faef9e5ad778d1788bc6

# 24 steps over three searches: from 0, from 3, and from 7, the end.
> deliver d1 to=search message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg search/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=41 alloc=500 state=500 end=return
run search/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=41 alloc=500
pumped state=idle fuel=41

> vars
vars search hits=[{text: "<a>", range: 1..3, captures: {}, ranges: {}}, {text: "<b>", range: 5..7, captures: {}, ranges: {}}]
